###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion: 

$\dfrac{\blueE{BP}}{BC}=\dfrac{BR}{BA}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{BP}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{BC}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{BP}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle RBP
\\
{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle A/\angle R}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{BP}}{BC}=\dfrac{BR}{BA}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{opposite to } \atop \angle C/\angle P}
\\
&\triangle ABC
\end{array}$
